{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "def:forget",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 0,
      "chapter": "0-corner",
      "source": "chapter/0-corner.tex",
      "line": 5,
      "title": "Forgetting a coordinate",
      "labels": [
        "def:forget"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [
        "NOF.forget"
      ],
      "leanok": true,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 0,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "For an index $i : [d]$, we define \\begin{align} \\forget_i : G^d & \\to G^{\\{j : [d] \\mid j \\ne i\\}} \\\\ x & \\mapsto j \\mapsto x_j \\end{align}"
    },
    {
      "id": "def:forbidden-pattern",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 1,
      "chapter": "0-corner",
      "source": "chapter/0-corner.tex",
      "line": 18,
      "title": "Forbidden pattern",
      "labels": [
        "def:forbidden-pattern"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [
        "NOF.IsForbiddenPatternWithTip",
        "NOF.IsForbiddenPattern"
      ],
      "leanok": true,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 1,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "We say a tuple $(a_1, \\dots, a_d) : (G^d)^d$ is a {\\bf forbidden pattern with tip $v : G^d$} if $$a_{i, j} = v_j$$ for all $i, j$ distinct. We also simply say $(a_1, \\dots, a_d)$ is a {\\bf forbidden pattern} if it is a forbidden pattern with tip $v$ for some $v$."
    },
    {
      "id": "def:multicorner",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 2,
      "chapter": "0-corner",
      "source": "chapter/0-corner.tex",
      "line": 29,
      "title": "Multidimensional corner",
      "labels": [
        "def:multicorner"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [
        "NOF.IsMultidimCorner"
      ],
      "leanok": true,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:forbidden-pattern"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 2,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "A {\\bf multidimensional corner} in $d$ dimensions is a tuple of the form $(x, x + ce_1, \\dots, x + ce_d)$ for some $x : G^d$ and $c : G$, where $ce_i$ is the vector of all zeroes except in position $i$ where it is $c$. Such a corner is said to be {\\bf trivial} if $c = 0$."
    },
    {
      "id": "def:corner-free-num",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 3,
      "chapter": "0-corner",
      "source": "chapter/0-corner.tex",
      "line": 38,
      "title": "Corner-free number",
      "labels": [
        "def:corner-free-num"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [],
      "leanok": false,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:multicorner"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 3,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "The {\\bf $d$-dimensional corner-free} number of $G$, denoted $r_d(G)$ is the size of the largest set $A$ in $G^d$ such that $A$ doesn't contain a non-trivial corner."
    },
    {
      "id": "def:corner-color-num",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 4,
      "chapter": "0-corner",
      "source": "chapter/0-corner.tex",
      "line": 47,
      "title": "Corner-coloring number",
      "labels": [
        "def:corner-color-num"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [],
      "leanok": false,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:multicorner"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 4,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "The {\\bf $d$-dimensional corner-coloring number} of $G$, denoted $\\chi_d(G)$, is the smallest number of colors one needs to color $G^d$ such that no non-trivial $d$-dimensional corner is monochromatic."
    },
    {
      "id": "lem:corner-num-lower",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "position": 5,
      "chapter": "0-corner",
      "source": "chapter/0-corner.tex",
      "line": 56,
      "title": "Lower bound on the corner-coloring number",
      "labels": [
        "lem:corner-num-lower"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [],
      "leanok": false,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:corner-free-num",
        "def:corner-color-num"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": true,
      "statement_event": 5,
      "proof_event": 6,
      "proof_chapter": "0-corner",
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "$$r_d(G) \\chi_d(G) \\ge N^d$$"
    },
    {
      "id": "lem:corner-num-upper",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "position": 6,
      "chapter": "0-corner",
      "source": "chapter/0-corner.tex",
      "line": 71,
      "title": "Upper bound on the corner-coloring number",
      "labels": [
        "lem:corner-num-upper"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [],
      "leanok": false,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:corner-free-num",
        "def:corner-color-num"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": true,
      "statement_event": 7,
      "proof_event": 8,
      "proof_chapter": "0-corner",
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "$$r_d(G) \\chi_d(G) \\le 2d N^d \\log N$$"
    },
    {
      "id": "def:protocol",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 7,
      "chapter": "1-nof-model",
      "source": "chapter/1-nof-model.tex",
      "line": 5,
      "title": "NOF protocol",
      "labels": [
        "def:protocol"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [
        "NOF.Protocol"
      ],
      "leanok": true,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 9,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "A {\\bf NOF protocol} $P$ consists of maps \\begin{align} \\strat : & [d] \\to G^{d - 1} \\to \\leanList \\Bool \\to \\Bool \\\\ \\guess : & [d] \\to G^{d - 1} \\to \\leanList \\Bool \\to \\Bool \\end{align}"
    },
    {
      "id": "def:broadcast",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 8,
      "chapter": "1-nof-model",
      "source": "chapter/1-nof-model.tex",
      "line": 19,
      "title": "NOF broadcast",
      "labels": [
        "def:broadcast"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [
        "NOF.Protocol.broadcast"
      ],
      "leanok": true,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:protocol",
        "def:forget"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 10,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "Given a NOF protocol $P$, the {\\bf NOF broadcast on input $x : G^d$} is inductively defined by \\begin{align} \\broad(x) : \\N & \\to \\leanList \\Bool \\\\ 0 & \\mapsto [] \\\\ t + 1 & \\mapsto \\strat_{t \\% d}(\\forget_{t \\% d}(x), \\broad(x, t)) :: \\broad(x, t) \\end{align}"
    },
    {
      "id": "lem:length-broadcast",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "position": 9,
      "chapter": "1-nof-model",
      "source": "chapter/1-nof-model.tex",
      "line": 33,
      "title": "Length of a broadcast",
      "labels": [
        "lem:length-broadcast"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [
        "NOF.Protocol.length_broadcast"
      ],
      "leanok": true,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:broadcast"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": true,
      "statement_event": 11,
      "proof_event": 12,
      "proof_chapter": "1-nof-model",
      "proof_leanok": true,
      "text": "For every NOF protocol $P$, every input $x : G^d$ and every time $t$, $\\broad(x, t)$ has length $t$."
    },
    {
      "id": "def:valid-protocol",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 10,
      "chapter": "1-nof-model",
      "source": "chapter/1-nof-model.tex",
      "line": 46,
      "title": "Valid NOF protocol",
      "labels": [
        "def:valid-protocol"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [
        "NOF.Protocol.IsValid"
      ],
      "leanok": true,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:broadcast"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 13,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "Given a function $F : G^d \\to \\Bool$, the NOF protocol $P$ is {\\bf valid in $F$ at time $t$ on input $x$} if all participants correctly guess $F(x)$, namely if $$\\guess_i(\\forget_i(x), \\broad(x, t)) = F(x)$$ for all $i : [d]$."
    },
    {
      "id": "def:trivial-protocol",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 11,
      "chapter": "1-nof-model",
      "source": "chapter/1-nof-model.tex",
      "line": 57,
      "title": "The trivial protocol",
      "labels": [
        "def:trivial-protocol"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [
        "NOF.Protocol.trivial"
      ],
      "leanok": false,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:protocol"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 14,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "For all $F$, we define the {\\bf trivial protocol} by making participant $i$ do \"Send the $t / d$-th bit of the number of participant $i + 1$\" and \"Compute $x_i$ from the binary representation given by participant $i - 1$, then compute $F(x)$\"."
    },
    {
      "id": "lem:trivial-protocol-valid",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "position": 12,
      "chapter": "1-nof-model",
      "source": "chapter/1-nof-model.tex",
      "line": 66,
      "title": "The trivial protocol is valid",
      "labels": [
        "lem:trivial-protocol-valid"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [],
      "leanok": false,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:valid-protocol",
        "def:trivial-protocol"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": true,
      "statement_event": 15,
      "proof_event": 16,
      "proof_chapter": "1-nof-model",
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "For all $F$, the trivial protocol for $F$ is valid in time $d\\ceil{\\log_2 n}$."
    },
    {
      "id": "def:det-protocol-complex",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 13,
      "chapter": "1-nof-model",
      "source": "chapter/1-nof-model.tex",
      "line": 80,
      "title": "Deterministic complexity of a protocol",
      "labels": [
        "def:det-protocol-complex"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [
        "NOF.Protocol.complexity"
      ],
      "leanok": true,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:valid-protocol"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 17,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "The {\\bf communication complexity of a NOF protocol $P$ for $F$} is the smallest time $t$ such that $P$ is valid in $F$ at time $t$ on all inputs $x$, or $\\infty$ if no such $t$ exists."
    },
    {
      "id": "def:det-fun-complex",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 14,
      "chapter": "1-nof-model",
      "source": "chapter/1-nof-model.tex",
      "line": 89,
      "title": "Deterministic complexity of a function",
      "labels": [
        "def:det-fun-complex"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [
        "NOF.funComplexity"
      ],
      "leanok": true,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:det-protocol-complex"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 18,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "The {\\bf deterministic communication complexity of a function} $F$, denoted $D(F)$, is the minimum of the communication complexity of $P$ when $P$ ranges over all NOF protocols."
    },
    {
      "id": "lem:trivial-bound-det-fun-complex",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "position": 15,
      "chapter": "1-nof-model",
      "source": "chapter/1-nof-model.tex",
      "line": 98,
      "title": "Trivial bound on the function complexity",
      "labels": [
        "lem:trivial-bound-det-fun-complex"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [],
      "leanok": false,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:det-fun-complex"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [
        "lem:trivial-protocol-valid"
      ],
      "has_proof": true,
      "statement_event": 19,
      "proof_event": 20,
      "proof_chapter": "1-nof-model",
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "The communication complexity of any function $F$ is at most $d\\ceil{\\log_2 n}$."
    },
    {
      "id": "lem:mono-forbidden-pattern-tip",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "position": 16,
      "chapter": "1-nof-model",
      "source": "chapter/1-nof-model.tex",
      "line": 113,
      "title": "The tip of a monochromatic forbidden pattern",
      "labels": [
        "lem:mono-forbidden-pattern-tip"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [
        "NOF.IsForbiddenPatternWithTip.broadcast_eq"
      ],
      "leanok": true,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:forbidden-pattern",
        "def:valid-protocol"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [
        "lem:length-broadcast"
      ],
      "has_proof": true,
      "statement_event": 21,
      "proof_event": 22,
      "proof_chapter": "1-nof-model",
      "proof_leanok": true,
      "text": "Given $P$ a NOF protocol and a time $t$, if $(a_1, \\dots, a_d)$ is a forbidden pattern with tip $v$ such that $\\broad(a_i, t)$ equals some fixed broadcast history $b$ for all $i$, then $\\broad(v, t) = b$ as well."
    },
    {
      "id": "def:eval",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 17,
      "chapter": "2-lower-bound-eval",
      "source": "chapter/2-lower-bound-eval.tex",
      "line": 3,
      "title": "$\\eval$ function",
      "labels": [
