    {
      "id": "def:non-monochromatic-protocol",
      "kind": "definition",
      "position": 22,
      "chapter": "3-upper-bound-eval",
      "source": "chapter/3-upper-bound-eval.tex",
      "line": 3,
      "title": "The non-monochromatic protocol",
      "labels": [
        "def:non-monochromatic-protocol"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [],
      "leanok": false,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:protocol"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 32,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "Given a coloring $c : \\{x \\mid \\eval x = 1\\} \\to [C]$, writing $a_i$ the vector whose $j$-th coordinate is $x_j$ except when $j = i$ in which case it is $-\\sum_{j \\ne i} x_j$, we define the {\\bf non-monochromatic protocol for $c$} by making participant $i$ do ``Send the $t / d$-th bit of $c(a_i)$ until time $\\lceil\\log_2\\chi_d(G)\\rceil$, then send $1$ iff $c(a_i)$ agrees with the broadcast from time $1$ to time $\\lceil\\log_2\\chi_d(G)\\rceil$ read as a color'' and ``Send $1$ iff the broadcasts from time $\\lceil\\log_2\\chi_d(G)\\rceil$ to time $\\lceil\\log_2\\chi_d(G)\\rceil + d$ were all $1$''."
    },
    {
      "id": "lem:non-monochromatic-protocol-valid",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "position": 23,
      "chapter": "3-upper-bound-eval",
      "source": "chapter/3-upper-bound-eval.tex",
      "line": 12,
      "title": "The non-monochromatic protocol is valid",
      "labels": [
        "lem:non-monochromatic-protocol-valid"
      ],
      "lean_decls": [],
      "leanok": false,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [
        "def:non-monochromatic-protocol",
        "def:valid-protocol"
      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": true,
      "statement_event": 33,
      "proof_event": 34,
      "proof_chapter": "3-upper-bound-eval",
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "If $c$ is a coloring such that all monochromatic forbidden patterns are trivial, then the non-monochromatic protocol for $c$ is valid in time $\\lceil\\log_2\\chi_d(G)\\rceil + d$."
    },
    {
      "id": "thm:det-fun-complex-eval-le-corner-color-num",
      "kind": "theorem",
